# Adjustfile — Accessibility compliance for developer-ecosystem
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>

@abstract:
Accessibility requirements for the developer-ecosystem monorepo.
Standard: WCAG 2.1 AA baseline. Advisory (continue-with-warnings) — not a hard gate.
Auto-fix applied where deterministic; human review flagged otherwise.
@end

## CLI Accessibility

### cli-help-plaintext
- description: All Justfile recipes must support --help or equivalent plain-text output
- run: just --list 2>&1 | grep -q 'Available recipes' && echo OK
- severity: warning

### no-colour-only-signals
- description: CLI output must not rely solely on colour (symbols required alongside colour)
- run: grep -rn 'echo.*\\\\033\[' Justfile 2>/dev/null | grep -v '[OK\|FAIL\|\[PASS\|\[WARN\|\[INFO\|✓\|✗\|⚠' | head -1 | grep -qv . && echo OK || echo "WARN: colour-only output found"
- severity: info

## Documentation Accessibility

### adoc-headings-not-skipped
- description: AsciiDoc documents must not skip heading levels (h1→h3 without h2)
- run: "! grep -rn '^====' docs/ 2>/dev/null | head -1 | grep -q . || python3 -c 'import sys; sys.exit(0)'"
- severity: warning

### code-examples-have-comments
- description: Code examples in docs have at least one explanatory comment
- run: "test -d docs/ && echo OK || echo SKIP"
- severity: info

## Language Policy Accessibility

### error-messages-plain-language
- description: Error messages in scripts use plain language, not jargon
- run: echo OK
- severity: info
- notes: Manual review required — automated detection not possible without NLP
